            <ArticleTitle>Dissecting hematoma of the thoracic aorta extending into a coronary artery: angiographic demonstration.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>329-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery dissection due to intramural extension from a dissecting hematoma of the aorta is an uncommon but well-recognized complication, occurring in 8% of a large pathological series. Angiographic demonstration of a case is presented and other causes of coronary artery dissection are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
